p;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td width="111" valign="top" style="border: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 14.2373%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 2.15pt 0 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt"&gt;34,303,574&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height: 6.0686%"&gt;&lt;td width="342" valign="top" style="border: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 60%"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0 38.15pt 0 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td width="118" valign="top" style="border-top: 3px none currentColor; border-right: 3px none currentColor; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 19.1525%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 5.05pt 0 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td width="20" valign="top" style="border: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 6.77966%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td width="111" valign="top" style="border-top: 3px none currentColor; border-right: 3px none currentColor; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 14.2373%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 2.15pt 0 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height: 11.8734%"&gt;&lt;td width="342" valign="top" style="border: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 60%"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0 38.15pt 0 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt"&gt;Net   Deferred Tax Liability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td width="118" valign="top" style="border-top: 3px none currentColor; border-right: 3px none currentColor; border-bottom: 1.5pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 19.1525%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 5.05pt 0 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt"&gt;$&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;35,407,040&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td width="20" valign="top" style="border: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 6.77966%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td width="111" valign="top" style="border-top: 3px none currentColor; border-right: 3px none currentColor; border-bottom: 1.5pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: 3px none currentColor; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 4.95pt; width: 14.2373%"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 2.15pt 0 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt"&gt;$&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;28,958,298&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;12.  Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On August 31, 2018, the Company entered an Engineering, Procurement and Construction (&amp;quot;EPC&amp;quot;) Agreement for the construction of TWL in the amount of $193 million with EC Source Services, LLC. On August 12, 2022, DCRT amended the original EPC contract with EC Source Services, LLC to increase the amount to $318 million. Throughout construction, nine change orders were issued increasing the EC Source Services, LLC total contract amount to $323 million. The agreement is a lump sum turnkey agreement and runs through construction to the final completion, which was obtained in August 2025. Retainage of 10% is withheld on the EPC Agreement. There was no retainage outstanding as of December 31, 2025 and 2024. Costs incurred under this contract amounted to $-0- and $60,303,131 for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively, and are included in Property, plant and equipment on the Balance Sheets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On August 30, 2018, the Company entered an Engineering, Design and Procurement Agreement for the interconnection of the Facility with Southern California Edison Company (&amp;quot;SCE&amp;quot;). Costs incurred under this contract amounted to $-0- and $10,107,620 for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively, and are included in Property, plant and equipment on the Balance Sheets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On June 1, 2023, the Company entered an Engineering, Design and Procurement Agreement for the construction and interconnection of the Cielo Azul Switchyard with Barnard Construction Inc. Costs incurred under this contract amounted to $-0- and $43,338,614 for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively, and are included in Property, plant and equipment on the Balance Sheets. Retainage of 10% was withheld on 50% of the contract and the retainage outstanding as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, was $-0- and $2,195,806, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Company is subject to property tax audits by various state and local taxing authorities, including California and Arizona, related primarily to assessed values for certain construction period and placed in service assets. Based on information currently available and in accordance with ASC 450, Contingencies, management has concluded that it is probable that additional property tax assessments will be incurred for these matters and that the amount of the assessment is reasonably estimable. Accordingly, as of December 31, 2025 the Company has recorded a liability of $16,683,954, which represents management's best estimate of the probable loss as of the balance sheet date. The ultimate resolution of these audits may differ from amounts accrued, and any such difference will be recognized in the period in which the matter is resolved or when additional information becomes available. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To the extent additional property tax assessments are ultimately incurred, the Company expects recovery of such amounts through regulatory mechanisms; however, regulatory recovery is not considered in determining the amount of the recorded liability.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;13.  Risks and Uncertainties&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pursuant to the APSA, DCRT is subject to a cost cap for certain portions of TWL; however, such costs exceeded this unadjusted cap materially. The route selected by the United States Department of the Interior, Bureau of Land Management (&amp;quot;BLM&amp;quot;) is approximately 11 miles longer than the original DCRT proposed route. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This increase in route length, along with different structure requirements, additional access roads, additional private property easements, and other unexpected mitigation requirements directed by the BLM, had an impact on TWL costs. Delays in the environmental permitting process (particularly the federal NEPA and state of California CEQA/CPCN processes) impacted the overall Project schedule and cost.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On March 16, 2020, DCRT notified the CAISO per Article 13 of the APSA that due to the pandemic caused by COVID-19, performance under the APSA will likely be impacted and delayed due to this force majeure event. Significant delays and related costs, such as those related to the delayed issuance of the Certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity (&amp;quot;CPCN&amp;quot;) by the California Public Utilities Commission, have been incurred. Such costs and their impacts are addressed in the FPA section 205 filing with FERC made by DCRT on June 29, 2023.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;14.  Asset Retirement Obligation (&amp;quot;ARO&amp;quot;)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Company has certain legal obligations related to the dismantlement, restoration, and abandonment of its electric transmission assets. These obligations generally arise when transmission lines, substations, or other equipment are placed in service. The Company is required to record an ARO for these obligations based on the fair value of the dismantlement, restoration, and abandonment costs expected to be incurred.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Quantified ARO&lt;br /&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company has recognized an ARO liability of $16,914,222 and $16,020,290, respectively, for the dismantlement and removal of certain transmission assets. This liability reflects the present value of the estimated future costs associated with the dismantlement, restoration, and abandonment of these assets. The estimate is based on current legal requirements, existing technology, and expected future costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unquantified ARO&lt;br /&gt;The Company also has additional AROs related to other electric transmission assets that have not been quantified due to significant uncertainty surrounding the timing and method of settlement of these obligations. The primary factors contributing to this uncertainty include the long-term nature of the obligations, potential changes in legal requirements, and the potential for technological advancements that may alter the expected costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Company is continuously evaluating its AROs and will recognize a liability when the fair value of the obligation can be reasonably estimated. Until such time, the Company will disclose the existence of these obligations and the factors contributing to the inability to quantify them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;15.  Subsequent Event&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Company has evaluated subsequent events for adjustment to or disclosure in its financial statements through April 29, 2026 and has not identified any subsequent events that require disclosure. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
